  "name": "FDP (FIBROGEN DEGRADATION PRODUCTS)",
  "code": "1549",
  "cost": 0,
  "interpretation": "<p data-start=\"95\" data-end=\"384\">Fibrinogen Degradation Products (FDPs) are fragments produced when <strong data-start=\"162\" data-end=\"201\">fibrinogen or fibrin is broken down</strong> by plasmin. This test helps detect abnormal clot breakdown (fibrinolysis) and is often used to evaluate <strong data-start=\"306\" data-end=\"354\">disseminated intravascular coagulation (DIC)</strong> and <strong data-start=\"359\" data-end=\"383\">thrombotic disorders</strong>.</p>\n<table>\n<thead>\n<tr>\n<th><strong>FDP Level</strong></th>\n<th><strong>Interpretation</strong></th>\n</tr>\n</thead>\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&lt;10 &micro;g/mL</strong></td>\n<td>Normal &mdash; no excessive fibrinolytic activity</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>10&ndash;40 &micro;g/mL</strong></td>\n<td>Mildly elevated &mdash; may indicate early fibrinolysis or resolving clot</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><strong>&gt;40 &micro;g/mL</strong></td>\n<td>Markedly elevated &mdash; suggests significant fibrinolysis as seen in:</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>- <strong>Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation (DIC)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>- <strong>Thromboembolic events (e.g., DVT, PE)</strong></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\n<td>- <strong>Severe trauma, surgery, or advanced liver disease</strong></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p data-start=\"1477\" data-end=\"1531\"><strong data-start=\"1481\" data-end=\"1531\">Clinical Conditions Associated with High FDPs:</strong></p>\n<ul data-start=\"1533\" data-end=\"1751\">\n<li data-start=\"1533\" data-end=\"1583\">\n<p data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1583\"><strong data-start=\"1535\" data-end=\"1583\">DIC (Disseminated Intravascular Coagulation)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1584\" data-end=\"1616\">\n<p data-start=\"1586\" data-end=\"1616\"><strong data-start=\"1586\" data-end=\"1616\">Deep Vein Thrombosis (DVT)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1617\" data-end=\"1646\">\n<p data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1646\"><strong data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1646\">Pulmonary Embolism (PE)</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1647\" data-end=\"1672\">\n<p data-start=\"1649\" data-end=\"1672\"><strong data-start=\"1649\" data-end=\"1672\">Post-surgical state</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1673\" data-end=\"1694\">\n<p data-start=\"1675\" data-end=\"1694\"><strong data-start=\"1675\" data-end=\"1694\">Liver cirrhosis</strong></p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1695\" data-end=\"1751\">\n<p data-start=\"1697\" data-end=\"1751\"><strong data-start=\"1697\" data-end=\"1751\">Placental abruption or preeclampsia (in pregnancy)</strong></p>\n</li>\n</ul>",
